{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110324","id":2807557203,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6nV-xT","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110324","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110324.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110324.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110324","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110324/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110324/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110324/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/7be003fc3ca0b18e0b30efd365eadf5264a77dc8","number":110324,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Improve the CPP dialect selection for Rider, when MSVC is not used (reverted)","user":{"login":"van800","id":1482681,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODI2ODE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1482681?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800","html_url":"https://github.com/van800","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/van800/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I was working on a gdextension on Mac and on the following code, I spotted couple of static analysis errors, which were caused by improper PlatformToolset. Decided to pull request to the main godotengine.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1246\" height=\"297\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5f7db628-b1e5-4249-a87c-1a3056f36e49\" />\r\n\r\n<details markdown=1>\r\n\r\n<summary>Code example</summary>\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\n#include <iostream>\r\n#include <vector>\r\n#include <string>\r\n#include <sstream>\r\n#include <unordered_map>\r\n#include <algorithm>\r\n#include <numeric>\r\n#include <optional>\r\n#include <random>\r\n#include <chrono>\r\n#include <cctype>\r\n\r\n// Demonstrates usage of several C++17 std library facilities in a small program.\r\n\r\nstatic std::unordered_map<std::string, int> word_count(const std::string& text) {\r\n    std::unordered_map<std::string, int> freq;\r\n    std::istringstream iss(text);\r\n    std::string w;\r\n    while (iss >> w) {\r\n        // normalize to lowercase and strip punctuation at ends\r\n        auto begin = std::find_if(w.begin(), w.end(), [](unsigned char c){ return std::isalnum(c); });\r\n        auto end = std::find_if(w.rbegin(), w.rend(), [](unsigned char c){ return std::isalnum(c); }).base();\r\n        if (begin < end) {\r\n            std::string norm(begin, end);\r\n            std::transform(norm.begin(), norm.end(), norm.begin(), [](unsigned char c){ return static_cast<char>(std::tolower(c)); });\r\n            ++freq[norm];\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n    return freq;\r\n}\r\n\r\nstatic std::vector<std::pair<std::string,int>> top_k(const std::unordered_map<std::string,int>& freq, std::size_t k) {\r\n    std::vector<std::pair<std::string,int>> items(freq.begin(), freq.end());\r\n    // sort by count desc, then word asc\r\n    std::sort(items.begin(), items.end(), [](const auto& a, const auto& b){\r\n        if (a.second != b.second) return a.second > b.second;\r\n        return a.first < b.first;\r\n    });\r\n    if (items.size() > k) items.resize(k);\r\n    return items;\r\n}\r\n\r\nstatic std::pair<double, std::optional<double>> sum_and_median(std::vector<int> values) {\r\n    if (values.empty()) return {0.0, std::nullopt};\r\n    // nth_element to find median in O(n)\r\n    std::size_t n = values.size();\r\n    std::nth_element(values.begin(), values.begin() + n/2, values.end());\r\n    if (n % 2 == 1) {\r\n        double med = values[n/2];\r\n        double sum = std::accumulate(values.begin(), values.end(), 0.0);\r\n        return {sum, med};\r\n    } else {\r\n        int a = values[n/2];\r\n        std::nth_element(values.begin(), values.begin() + n/2 - 1, values.end());\r\n        int b = values[n/2 - 1];\r\n        double med = (a + b) / 2.0;\r\n        double sum = std::accumulate(values.begin(), values.end(), 0.0);\r\n        return {sum, med};\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n\r\nint main(int argc, char** argv) {\r\n    std::cout << \"Hello from HelloGnuMake sample!\\n\";\r\n\r\n    // 1) Use std to analyze text\r\n    const std::string text = \"C++ makes it easy to shoot yourself in the foot; std makes it harder, but when you do, it blows your whole leg off.\";\r\n    auto freq = word_count(text);\r\n    auto top3 = top_k(freq, 3);\r\n\r\n    std::cout << \"Top 3 words:\\n\";\r\n    for (const auto& item : top3) {\r\n        const auto& w = item.first;\r\n        int c = item.second;\r\n        std::cout << \"  '\" << w << \"' -> \" << c << \"\\n\";\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    // 2) Use random + algorithms to process numbers\r\n    std::optional<unsigned int> seed;\r\n    if (argc > 1) {\r\n    \t// fails with emcc\r\n        // try {\r\n        //     unsigned int s = static_cast<unsigned int>(std::stoul(argv[1]));\r\n        //     seed = std::make_optional(s);\r\n        // } catch (...) {}\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    std::mt19937 rng;\r\n    if (seed) {\r\n        rng.seed(*seed);\r\n        std::cout << \"Using user-provided seed: \" << *seed << \"\\n\";\r\n    } else {\r\n        auto now = static_cast<unsigned int>(std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now().time_since_epoch().count());\r\n        rng.seed(now);\r\n        std::cout << \"Using time-based seed.\\n\";\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    std::uniform_int_distribution<int> dist(1, 100);\r\n    std::vector<int> values;\r\n    values.resize(20);\r\n    std::generate(values.begin(), values.end(), [&]{ return dist(rng); });\r\n\r\n    // transform: square odd numbers, keep even as-is\r\n    std::transform(values.begin(), values.end(), values.begin(), [](int x){ return (x % 2) ? x*x : x; });\r\n\r\n    auto result = sum_and_median(values);\r\n    double sum = result.first;\r\n    auto median = result.second;\r\n\r\n    std::cout << \"Values: \";\r\n    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < values.size(); ++i) {\r\n        if (i) std::cout << \", \";\r\n        std::cout << values[i];\r\n    }\r\n    std::cout << \"\\n\";\r\n\r\n    std::cout << \"Sum: \" << sum << \"\\n\";\r\n    if (median) std::cout << \"Median: \" << *median << \"\\n\";\r\n    else std::cout << \"Median: n/a\\n\";\r\n\r\n    return 0;\r\n}\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n*Production edit:* add code highlight and code example in details tag.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098009,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwMDk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:buildsystem","name":"topic:buildsystem","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/23","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23/labels","number":23,"state":"closed","title":"4.6","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_i